"ADDENDUM (mhp/mep side effect): apply_stat_block's writes mostly vanish — attack/defense/appearance become direct reads of the per-group totals. The ONE genuine side effect, the mhp/mep ratchet (raising current hp/ep to carry the new max), moves to systems via the per-tick transient-component feature (dev-per-tick-transient-state): when the core/stats total system recomputes, it records a transient mhp component (and mep); a separate system applies the mhp delta to hp wherever that transient exists (ratchet: only raise; carry current hp up by the increase), same for mep->ep. The transient is single-tick and self-clearing, so no cleanup and no ordering coupling beyond running the applier after the stats-total system. Keeps the stats-total system a pure value producer; the hp/ep mutation lives in its own applier system."